# inc-ympc: the Spell Manager shows each held source in a Src column and no
# spell list prefixes the name with "(arc)". Read by tools/check_spell_tags.sh.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/human-priest-mage-dual-seed4-gate.sav \
#   INCURSION_CHAR_PROBE=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/spell-tags.keys 4
#
# THE CHARACTER. Kethad, the frozen Priest 1 / Mage 1 who holds Protection from
# Evil from BOTH sources (arcane=1 divine=1), saved in wizard mode at depth 2,
# already rested.
#
# THE ROUTE (each @dump label is one assertion screen in the check):
#   1. 's' searches: one real turn, so the session counts as gameplay.
#   2. 'm' opens the cast menu (the Spell Manager): the two versions
#      of Protection from Evil read "Protection from Evil   arc" and
#      "Protection from Evil   div".                          cast-menu
#   3. 'd' opens the character sheet, 'L' the Learn Spells
#      checklist: the Source column reads Arcane and Divine.  learn-spells
#   4. ESC, ESC return to play; ESC opens the System Menu, 'b' is
#      Save and Continue, which (under INCURSION_CHAR_PROBE=1)
#      writes logs/charprobe.txt -- the character sheet's full
#      "Known Spells" dump, where the two bare-name lines show.  saved
#
# Keys that bite: the checklist is reached from the character sheet with 'L'
# (see tools/keys/mage-loadout-rest.keys). Lowercase 'd' is the character
# sheet. The cast menu is 'm'. The character sheet has no "Things in View"
# line, so no @until guard is used on it. ESC on the sheet returns to play;
# ESC in play opens the System Menu (see tools/keys/load-char-sheet.keys).

s

m
@dump:cast-menu
ESC

d
L
@dump:learn-spells
ESC
ESC

ESC
@expect "System Menu"
b
@dump:saved
